---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

import { PRIVACY_EMAIL } from '../../data/pantrybaby';

// Facts verified against the BudgetBaby source on 2026-10-20 (CRM launch validation, D-10).
const lastUpdated = 'October 20, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="BudgetBaby Privacy Policy"
  description="BudgetBaby privacy policy: what data is collected, what is not collected, how data is stored, and your rights."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/privacy"
>
  <div class="policy-layout">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <div class="policy-header">
        <a href="/budgetbaby" class="policy-back">← BudgetBaby</a>
        <div class="label-chip" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">Legal</div>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated} · Applies to BudgetBaby for iOS</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-summary glass">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your budget data lives on your device. Cloud Sync is off unless you turn it on.</li>
          <li>Backups are encrypted on your device before they are saved or uploaded. We cannot read them.</li>
          <li>Crash reports and usage data help us fix and improve the app. Turn them off in Settings, then Privacy, then Analytics &amp; Crash Reports. We never track you across other apps.</li>
          <li>We don't sell data, serve ads, or connect to your bank.</li>
          <li>Delete your data or account in Settings, then Account, then Danger Zone.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-content">

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
          <p>When you use BudgetBaby without an account, we collect nothing. Your data is entirely local.</p>
          <p>When you create an account or use cloud features, we collect:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address and display name. If you use Sign in with Apple, Apple may provide a relay email. We never see your real email unless you choose to share it.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud backup data.</strong> If you create a cloud backup, your budget data, encrypted with AES-256-GCM before it leaves your device. We cannot decrypt or read your backup data.</li>
            <li><strong>Synced data.</strong> If you turn on Cloud Sync (Settings, then Account), your budget data is stored in your account so it appears on your other devices. Synced data is encrypted in transit and at rest by Google, but it is not end-to-end encrypted.</li>
            <li><strong>Authentication tokens.</strong> Secure tokens used to verify your identity with Firebase Auth. These are stored in the iOS Keychain.</li>
            <li><strong>Subscription status.</strong> Whether your account has an active Premium subscription, as verified by RevenueCat. We store this in the iOS Keychain, not on our servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Crash reports.</strong> Crash reports via Firebase Crashlytics to help us fix bugs. They contain technical details about the crash and your device, never your financial data. If you are signed in, they are linked to your account ID. On by default; turn off with Analytics &amp; Crash Reports.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage data.</strong> Which features you use (for example "logged a transaction", with the category you chose), sent to our own servers. If you are signed in it is linked to your BabyBlocks account. No amounts or account numbers. On by default; turn off with Analytics &amp; Crash Reports.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>2. What we do not collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>The contents of your budget, including transactions, amounts, categories, or any financial data, unless you enable cloud backup.</li>
            <li>Bank account numbers, credit card numbers, or any payment credentials.</li>
            <li>Location data.</li>
            <li>Contacts or calendar data, except when you use the optional Calendar Sync feature, which reads and writes only to your iOS Calendar with your explicit permission.</li>
            <li>Your name or personal identity beyond what you provide during account creation.</li>
            <li>Advertising identifiers. BudgetBaby does not track you across other companies' apps or websites.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>3. How your data is stored</h2>

          <h3>On-device storage</h3>
          <p>
            All budget data is stored locally on your device using SwiftData. It is encrypted by iOS device
            encryption at rest. We have no access to locally stored data under any circumstances.
          </p>

          <h3>Cloud backup</h3>
          <p>Cloud backup is entirely opt-in. If you choose to enable it, here is exactly what happens:</p>
          <ol class="policy-steps">
            <li>
              <strong>Encryption on your device.</strong> Before any data leaves your phone, BudgetBaby encrypts
              it using AES-256-GCM. This happens locally, before any network request is made.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Key storage in iCloud Keychain.</strong> The encryption key is generated on your device
              and stored in your iOS Keychain, which syncs via iCloud Keychain. We never have access to the key.
              Without the key, the encrypted data is unreadable, including by us.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Encrypted upload over TLS.</strong> The already-encrypted backup file is transmitted
              over a TLS connection to Firebase Storage. It is stored there scoped to your user account.
              No other user can access your storage path.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Restore on a new device.</strong> When you restore, your device fetches the encrypted file,
              retrieves the key from iCloud Keychain, decrypts locally, and loads your data. The decryption
              never happens on a server. It happens on your device.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Free accounts have one backup slot. Premium accounts have multiple named backup slots and the ability
            to schedule automatic backups.
          </p>

          <h3>Authentication data</h3>
          <p>
            Firebase Auth stores your email address and authentication credentials according to Google's Firebase
            privacy policies. Authentication tokens on your device are stored in the iOS Keychain.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>4. Forms and in-app communications</h2>
          <p>Here is a full list of every place BudgetBaby or this website collects information you provide directly.</p>

          <h3>Account creation (in-app)</h3>
          <p>
            When you create an account inside BudgetBaby, we collect your email address and a display name.
            These are stored via Firebase Auth. You can also sign in with Apple or Google, in which case your
            credentials are handled by Apple or Google respectively and we receive only what those platforms
            pass to us (typically an email and a user identifier).
          </p>

          <h3>Support contact</h3>
          <p>
            You can contact support in the app (Settings, then Support) or by email at
            <a href="mailto:budgetbaby@babyblocks.io">budgetbaby@babyblocks.io</a>. With a request we receive what you
            write, your email (or an anonymous identifier made from your device if you are not signed in), and your
            device model and iOS and app versions. If you attach a diagnostics report it contains technical logs and
            device details such as locale, time zone and currency. Screenshots or recordings you attach are sent as you
            chose them. We use this only to help you. We do not add you to any mailing list.
          </p>

          <h3>Notification waitlists (coming soon pages)</h3>
          <p>
            The website has waitlist pages for upcoming apps like PantryBaby. Those signup forms collect your
            name and email address only, used to send you a single notification email when the app launches.
            Each form makes clear exactly what you are signing up for before you submit it. You can ask us to
            remove your details at any time at support@babyblocks.io.
          </p>

          <h3>Feature requests</h3>
          <p>
            Our <a href="/coming-soon/feature-requests">public feature request board</a> is hosted by us at
            babyblocks.io. Submissions go directly to our backend (Cloudflare Workers + Firebase).
            We collect the title, description, app, and an optional email address (if you provide one)
            so we can ask follow-up questions. Submissions are reviewed manually before they appear on
            the public list. The same Privacy Policy that covers the rest of the site applies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
          <p>BudgetBaby uses the following third-party services. We name them here because you deserve to know exactly what is running in the app.</p>
          <div class="policy-table-wrap">
            <table class="policy-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Service</th>
                  <th>Purpose</th>
                  <th>Data shared</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Firebase Auth (Google)</td>
                  <td>Account authentication and identity</td>
                  <td>Account email, authentication tokens</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Firebase Firestore (Google)</td>
                  <td>Cloud sync (optional)</td>
                  <td>Sync data, encrypted in transit via TLS, stored encrypted at rest</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Firebase Storage (Google)</td>
                  <td>Cloud backup storage</td>
                  <td>Encrypted backup files (we cannot decrypt them)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Firebase Crashlytics (Google)</td>
                  <td>Crash reporting and stability monitoring</td>
                  <td>Crash logs, device model, iOS and app version, account ID if signed in</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Cloudflare (our servers at babyblocks.io)</td>
                  <td>Support requests and usage data</td>
                  <td>Support messages and diagnostics, usage events</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Microsoft 365</td>
                  <td>Support email</td>
                  <td>Emails you send us and our replies</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>RevenueCat</td>
                  <td>Subscription management</td>
                  <td>Subscription status, Apple-provided purchase receipts</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Apple StoreKit</td>
                  <td>In-app purchases</td>
                  <td>Purchase receipts processed and held by Apple</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Sign in with Apple</td>
                  <td>Federated authentication</td>
                  <td>Apple-controlled identity token. Your email is optional and may be relayed</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Sign in with Google</td>
                  <td>Federated authentication</td>
                  <td>Google account email and profile (limited scope, read-only)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>We do not sell your data to third parties. We do not use your data for advertising.</p>
          <p>
            Backups are encrypted on your device, so Google cannot read them. Synced data is protected by Google's
            encryption but is not end-to-end encrypted. If that is a concern, leave Cloud Sync off or use BudgetBaby
            without an account.
          </p>

          <h3>Data Processing Agreements</h3>
          <p>
            Google processes data on our behalf under their <a href="https://firebase.google.com/terms/data-processing-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Data Processing and Security Terms</a>,
            which incorporate Standard Contractual Clauses for international data transfers. RevenueCat processes
            subscription data under their <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/dpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data Processing Agreement</a>.
            These agreements ensure that our third-party processors handle your data in compliance with GDPR and other applicable data protection regulations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>6. Your rights and choices</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Access.</strong> You can export all your budget data in CSV or PDF format (Premium) at any time from within the app.</li>
            <li><strong>Deletion.</strong> In Settings, then Account, then Danger Zone: "Delete All Data" removes your cloud data and the data on this device and keeps your account; "Delete Account" removes your cloud data, your BabyBlocks account (which PantryBaby also uses) and the data on this device. Deleting does not cancel a subscription; cancel in your Apple ID settings. In-app deletion does not remove support requests, usage data or subscription records on our servers or at RevenueCat; email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a> to have those deleted.</li>
            <li><strong>Crash reports and usage data.</strong> Turn them off in Settings, then Privacy, then Analytics &amp; Crash Reports.</li>
            <li><strong>Portability.</strong> Your exported CSV data is in standard human-readable format compatible with any spreadsheet application.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>For users in the European Economic Area (EEA)</h3>
          <p>
            If you are located in the EEA, you have additional rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), including the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing of, and port your personal data. You also have the right to withdraw consent at any time and to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our legal bases are contract (your account, Cloud Sync, backups and subscription) and legitimate interest (crash reports, usage data and answering support requests), which you can object to at any time by turning off Analytics &amp; Crash Reports or emailing us.
          </p>

          <h3 id="ccpa-do-not-sell">For users in California</h3>
          <p>
            If you are a California resident, you have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), including the right to know what personal information we collect, the right to request deletion, and the right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information.</strong> We do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising, and we have not done so in the preceding twelve months. The CCPA requires us to make this disclosure clear and conspicuous, which is why this section exists and why a permanent link to it lives in the site footer. To exercise any privacy right (access, correction, deletion, portability, or opt-out), email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>. We respond within 30 days and do not require an account to make a request.
          </p>

          <h3>Cookies</h3>
          <p>
            This website does not use cookies. The BudgetBaby app does not use cookies. No tracking cookies, advertising cookies, or third-party cookies are set by any of our properties.
          </p>

          <h3>Data retention</h3>
          <p>
            Local data remains on your device until you delete it. Synced data and cloud backups stay while your account exists and are deleted when you delete them in the app. Crash reports are kept by Firebase Crashlytics for up to 90 days. Support requests and usage data are kept until you ask us to delete them. Support reports saved on your device are removed after 90 days.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>BudgetBaby is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information, email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>If we make material changes to this policy, we'll update the "last updated" date and notify users within the app. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>9. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy-related questions, data access requests, or to exercise any of your rights described above,
            email us at <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Data Controller:</strong><br />
            Intrigue MMC LLC, operating as Intriguing Insight<br />
            Privacy contact: <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-layout {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-12));
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .policy-back {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .policy-back:hover { color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
  }

  .policy-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-meta {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-summary {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .policy-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-10);
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-section h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .policy-section ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .policy-steps {
    list-style: decimal;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-steps li { padding-left: var(--space-2); }

  .policy-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
  }

  .policy-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }

  .policy-table th {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .policy-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .policy-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
</style>
